+def scout_past_tests(tree: ast.Module) -> ast.Module:
+    """Rewrite a statement for the scout so that a test on a result does not end it.
+
+    The scout places no bets: where an `if` needs a value that is not there yet, it
+    stops, and with it the loop the `if` is in (ScoutStop). But a test whose arms cannot
+    leave that loop (no return, raise, break, continue or assert in them) changes
+    nothing about what comes after it: the loop goes on whichever arm runs. Recorded on
+    OOLONG: a loop of 160 batches that counts each label with `if label == 'location':`.
+    Every one of those batches is certain, and neither spec-ptc as shipped nor the scout
+    launched them ahead.
+
+    So such an `if` becomes: work out the test; if that needs an unknown value, run
+    neither arm and make every name an arm sets or changes unknown; else run the `if`
+    as written. A call inside a skipped arm is not launched (that would be a bet), and
+    a later call built from a name an arm sets is not launched either. A test inside a
+    function or class body is left as it is."""
+    tree = _PastTests().visit(tree)
+    return ast.fix_missing_locations(tree)
+
